From f1e92eff7b2334f10b10895f2ab1c5d1dba738ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:47:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 43/50] drm/gma500: make the sgxfive render node opt-in

Client GPU programs can read every SGX register, including the physical
address of a page directory, and temporaries that earlier tasks left
behind, so the render node is for trusted users only. Add the module
parameter sgx_render, off by default and read-only at runtime. When it is
off, psb_init() drops DRIVER_RENDER from the drm_driver so no render node
is created: drm_dev_init() already allocates the render minor from the
driver's features, so masking drm_device.driver_features before
drm_dev_register() would be too late. The primary node goes to the seat
user and the compositor, who are not trusted either, so it then accepts
only DEV_QUERY and returns -EPERM for every other sgxfive ioctl. With the
parameter on nothing changes. KUnit covers the ioctl gate.

Assisted-by: LLM
